  "live_records": {
    "q-12546": {
      "dom_id": "step-q12546",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14255079/assets/c072e1deff8c28feea3810c35b4d4fc4bae92e56f4eedebb73bf4e6f8831372d.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the equation of the graph shown above?",
      "worked_solution": "Let's add the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ to the plot.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14255079/assets/9d347014b124c5496ea1bdb6b2039a7ddbf2349ac4260b902afe98f2664ad38e.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$\n\n- Then, shift it by $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ units **left.**\n\nTherefore, the given graph is $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{2})$",
