      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14255079/assets/40322f60d8d97a7c8beff78627e78bf730be621675300b897b636a1e7d4979cf.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the equation of the graph shown above?",
      "worked_solution": "Let's add the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ to the plot.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14255079/assets/07415c592730ede309f0ba0979d203337e4cfcf2ebfa3b7215a27cedf7f6673f.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$\n\n- Then, shift it by $\\frac{3}{2}$ units **left.**\n\nTherefore, the given graph is $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+\\frac{3}{2}).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
